= Solution
{parent=10}

On the disc $z=0$, the upward normal selects only the third component, which equals $e^0/(1+0)=1$. Hence the <surface integral> is the area of the <unit disk>:
$$
\boxed{\int_D\boldsymbol F\cdot\boldsymbol n\,dS
=\int_D1\,dS=\pi.}
$$

